{# ============================================================
   ONE SPECIMEN (#201)

   Renders the block it is called with twice: once live, once as its
   own source. The second pass is what makes the gallery answerable
   rather than merely pretty, because the question it gets asked is
   "what do I write to get that", and reading it off the page beats
   hunting for the one screen that already uses it.

   caller() is evaluated both times, so a specimen must not depend on
   anything that changes between the two. Static markup only, which is
   all any of these are.

   dedent strips the indent this file's own {% call %} block adds; see
   scripts/build.mjs. forceescape and not escape, because a macro's
   output arrives marked safe and plain escape would pass it straight
   through as live markup inside the <pre>.
   ============================================================ #}

{% macro story(title, note='') %}
<article class="sg-story">
  <h3 class="sg-story-title">{{ title }}</h3>
  {% if note %}
  <p class="sg-story-note">{{ note }}</p>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="sg-specimen">
{{ caller() }}
  </div>
  <details class="sg-source">
    <summary>Markup</summary>
    <pre><code>{{ caller() | dedent | forceescape }}</code></pre>
  </details>
</article>
{% endmacro %}
